<title>JAPAN: Shinpo to buy back shares for stock option.</title>
<headline>Shinpo to buy back shares for stock option.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Shinpo Co Ltd said on Thursday that it plans to buy back up to 100 million yen worth of its shares, or up to 100,000 shares, in order to introduce a stock option scheme.</p>
<p>The specialised maker of smokeless meat roasters for restaurants said in a statement that its board had decided to introduce a stock option programme for company executives.</p>
</text>
